{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold \"stitch\" task (#5135) to implement srd007-sponge R6.1 and R6.2 requirements. The task requires modifying two files (`cmd/sponge/main.go` and `cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go`) to add differential testing capabilities that compare output file content between the Go implementation and the reference `sponge` binary from Homebrew moreutils. The task is part of an automated code generation pipeline (generation run 44), and git operations are managed externally by the orchestrator.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `testutils.DiffTest` struct\n   - `DiffTest.ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte` field for file-content comparison\n   - sponge utility: reads all stdin before writing to output file (soak-before-write pattern)\n   - Append mode (`-a` flag): prepends original file content before stdin content\n   - Passthrough mode: writes to stdout when no output filename given\n   - Temp file spill: for large inputs exceeding memory threshold\n   - Cross-device rename fallback: when atomic rename fails across filesystems\n   - File mode preservation: output file retains permissions of original file\n   - Reference binary: `sponge` (not g-prefixed, from Homebrew moreutils)\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd007-sponge.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for R6.1 and R6.2 requirements\n     - R6.1: \"Differential tests must compare the content of the output file (not stdout) after both the Go binary and the reference binary have exited, using file-content comparison provided by pkg/testutils.\"\n     - R6.2: \"Tests must