{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SypTntXnQPp3tcMMJmBLpP","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information you requested. Here's my comprehensive report:\n\n## pkg/testutils Package Analysis\n\n### 1. DiffTest Struct Definition (Full)\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5135/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` lines 46-55:\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string\n\tArgs          []string\n\tStdin         []byte\n\tEnv           []string\n\tWorkDir       string\n\tExitCode      int\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n```\n\n**Field Meanings:**\n- **Name**: Identifies the subtest (used with t.Run)\n- **Args**: Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n- **Stdin**: Input to both binaries. nil means EOF immediately; empty []byte{} produces no bytes but with an open stdin. Defaults to nil.\n- **Env**: Environment variables. nil means inherit test process environment with LC_ALL=C applied as default override. Non-nil slices are merged: matching keys override inherited values, new keys are added.\n- **WorkDir**: Working directory for binary execution. If empty string, defaults to t.TempDir()\n- **ExitCode**: Expected exit code. Defaults to 0 when zero value is used.\n- **Normalize**: Slice of NormalizeFunc applied in order to stdout and stderr before comparison. Nil or empty means no normalization.\n- **ExpectedFiles**: Map of relative file paths to expected byte contents for file-content verification\n\n### 2. RunDiffTests Function Signature and Implementation\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5135/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` lines 83-105:\n\n```go\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tfor _, tc := range tests {\n\t\tt.Run(tc.Name, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\trunSubtest(t, goBinary, refBinary, tc)\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc runSubtest(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tc DiffTest) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tworkDir := tc.WorkDir\n\tif workDir == \"\" {\n\t\tworkDir = t.TempDir()\n\t}\n\tenv := buildEnv(tc.Env)\n\tgoRes := runBinary(t, goBinary, tc.Args, tc.Stdin, env, workDir)\n\trefRes := runBinary(t, refBinary, tc.Args, tc.Stdin, env, workDir)\n\tgoRes = applyNormalizers(goRes, tc.Normalize)\n\trefRes = applyNormalizers(refRes, tc.Normalize)\n\tcompareOutputs(t, tc, goRes, refRes)\n\tcheckExpectedFiles(t, workDir, tc.ExpectedFiles)\n}\n```\n\n**How File-Content Comparison Works (lines 211-227):**\n\n```go\nfunc checkExpectedFiles(t *testing.T, workDir string, expected map[string][]byte) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tif expected == nil {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tfor relPath, want := range expected {\n\t\tfullPath := filepath.Join(workDir, relPath)\n\t\tgot, err := os.ReadFile(fullPath)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"expected file %s: %v\", relPath, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !bytes.Equal(got, want) {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"file %s divergence\\n  expected: %q\\n  actual:   %q\",\n\t\t\t\trelPath, want, got)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThe ExpectedFiles comparison is **separate from stdout/stderr comparison**. It:\n1. Iterates over the ExpectedFiles map\n2. Joins each relative path with the workDir to get the full path\n3. Reads the actual file using os.ReadFile\n4. Compares actual content with expected content using bytes.Equal\n5. Fails the test if file doesn't exist OR content doesn't match\n\n**Stdout/Stderr Comparison (lines 176-185):**\n\n```go\nfunc compareOutputs(t *testing.T, tc DiffTest, goRes, refRes binaryResult) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tstdoutMatch := bytes.Equal(goRes.stdout, refRes.stdout)\n\tstderrMatch := bytes.Equal(goRes.stderr, refRes.stderr)\n\texitMatch := goRes.exitCode == refRes.exitCode\n\tif stdoutMatch && stderrMatch && exitMatch {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tt.Fatalf(\"%s\", formatDivergence(tc, goRes, refRes))\n}\n```\n\nThis compares the Go binary's output against the reference binary's output—both must match exactly (after normalization) for the test to pass.\n\n### 3. BuildBinary Function\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5135/pkg/testutils/build.go` lines 16-27:\n\n```go\nfunc BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tname := resolvePackageName(dir)\n\ttmpDir := t.TempDir()\n\tbinPath := filepath.Join(tmpDir, name)\n\tcmd := exec.Command(\"go\", \"build\", \"-o\", binPath, dir)\n\toutput, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"BuildBinary: go build %s failed: %v\\n%s\", dir, err, output)\n\t}\n\treturn binPath\n}\n```\n\n**Function Behavior:**\n- Takes a directory path (e.g., \"../../cmd/cat\")\n- Resolves the package name from the directory\n- Creates a temporary directory via t.TempDir()\n- Runs `go build -o <binPath> <dir>`\n- Returns the path to the compiled binary\n- Fails the test fatally if the build fails, printing combined stdout/stderr output\n\n**Helper function** `resolvePackageName` (lines 29-38):\n```go\nfunc resolvePackageName(dir string) string {\n\tif dir == \".\" {\n\t\tabs, err := filepath.Abs(dir)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"testbin\"\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn filepath.Base(abs)\n\t}\n\treturn filepath.Base(dir)\n}\n```\n\nUses the base directory name as the binary name (e.g., \"cat\" from \"cmd/cat\"). For \".\" it tries to resolve the absolute path; on error it defaults to \"testbin\"."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2d2b500-2c88-4156-9136-a8a376bfff58","uuid":"0092b755-22f7-4c04-9e72-c38e695cf339","timestamp":"2026-05-14T03:25:24.864Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5135, I need to understand the `pkg/testutils` package. Specifically:\n\n1. Read the full contents of all Go files in `pkg/testutils/`\n2. Find the `DiffTest` struct definiti